# GetGrocery — fresh groceries, delivered in Dublin (Kiosk demo)

AI assistants: start at [/.well-known/kiosk.json](/.well-known/kiosk.json) and read it with the skill at <<%= Kiosk.configuration.skill_url %>>.

## Try it with your own assistant

Tell your AI assistant: "Order milk, eggs and cheese from getgrocery.demo.kiosk.tech and check out."

It finds this store, registers itself, shops, books a delivery slot and pays. When it gives you the Stripe checkout link, pay with the test card 4242 4242 4242 4242, any future expiry, any CVC, any ZIP. Payment runs on real Stripe in test mode: no real money moves.

## About this demo

getgrocery is a demo grocery shop. An assistant does the whole order through Kiosk: find the shop, register, shop, book a delivery, pay. The customer saves a card with Stripe once, and the shop charges it later. The assistant never sees a card number.

- Source: <https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-getgrocery>
